WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.277 --> 00:00:03.615
- I can't wear fragrance
because I have sensitive skin.

00:00:03.615 --> 00:00:05.039
If I could, (man laughing) I wouldn't mind

00:00:05.039 --> 00:00:07.416
like a grilled meat fragrance.

00:00:07.416 --> 00:00:08.249
I really love it.

00:00:08.249 --> 00:00:11.999
(funky, bass-thumping music)

00:00:14.161 --> 00:00:14.994
- Hey, guys!

00:00:14.994 --> 00:00:16.613
In college, I used to work at Chipotle.

00:00:16.613 --> 00:00:19.498
Today, I'm bringing Chipotle to BuzzFeed.

00:00:19.498 --> 00:00:21.124
That's right, I'm bringing my burrito hack

00:00:21.124 --> 00:00:22.911
straight to my co-workers
to see what they think.

00:00:22.911 --> 00:00:26.582
I honestly think it is the
best combination of sweet,

00:00:26.582 --> 00:00:28.802
savory, salty, spicy,

00:00:28.802 --> 00:00:29.657
and

00:00:29.657 --> 00:00:31.488
chipotle all in one.

00:00:31.488 --> 00:00:35.155
(rhythmic, energetic music)

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:42.347
(rhythmic, energetic music)

00:00:43.754 --> 00:00:44.672
- Exactly, man.

00:00:44.672 --> 00:00:47.837
See, I come here all the time.

00:00:47.837 --> 00:00:48.836
- Damn right it does.

00:00:48.836 --> 00:00:52.503
(rhythmic, energetic music)

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:56.790
- Chipotle is probably my
favorite place in the world.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.547
For a long time, I think my record was

00:00:58.547 --> 00:01:00.741
I went 26 times in a month.

00:01:00.741 --> 00:01:01.574
- What!

00:01:01.574 --> 00:01:02.691
- I think that's the best I ever did.

00:01:02.691 --> 00:01:03.870
- That's almost every single day.

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:06.848
- My Chipotle opinion is
that Dos Toros is better.

00:01:06.848 --> 00:01:08.596
- No offense to Dos Toros but

00:01:08.596 --> 00:01:09.925
you can't replace Chipotle.

00:01:09.925 --> 00:01:13.842
(funky, rhythmic guitar music)

00:01:49.719 --> 00:01:53.817
(funky, rhythmic bass-thumping music)

00:01:53.817 --> 00:01:55.271
- [Woman] Oh, damn!

00:01:55.271 --> 00:01:57.639
- There Is a lot of guac in here.

00:01:57.639 --> 00:01:59.503
- Yeah, there's a (beeping) lot of guac.

00:01:59.503 --> 00:02:00.336
- Geez.

00:02:00.336 --> 00:02:01.239
- I know guac is extra.

00:02:01.239 --> 00:02:02.072
I never forget

00:02:02.072 --> 00:02:03.494
so this is a treat.

00:02:03.494 --> 00:02:04.806
- They won't let you forget.

00:02:04.806 --> 00:02:05.910
(laughing)

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:07.772
- It looks like something I would eat

00:02:07.772 --> 00:02:08.928
by myself.

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:10.442
- I just wanna know what
to do with this lemon.

00:02:10.442 --> 00:02:11.275
Is it like a shot?

00:02:11.275 --> 00:02:13.531
Do you take a bite then
you suck on the lemon

00:02:13.531 --> 00:02:14.628
like tequila?
- No.

00:02:14.628 --> 00:02:15.461
- No.

00:02:15.461 --> 00:02:16.746
- Before you take a bite,

00:02:16.746 --> 00:02:18.952
you must squeeze the
lemon unto the burrito.

00:02:18.952 --> 00:02:20.544
(hammer pounding)
Squeeze, eat, repeat.

00:02:20.544 --> 00:02:21.949
- I'm impressed 'cause a lifetime

00:02:21.949 --> 00:02:23.238
of drinking lemon water there

00:02:23.238 --> 00:02:25.594
and I never thought the lemon
would be part of the meal.

00:02:25.594 --> 00:02:26.498
- I'm nervous.

00:02:26.498 --> 00:02:28.268
- So squeeze.

00:02:28.268 --> 00:02:29.351
- It's going everywhere.

00:02:29.351 --> 00:02:30.297
Ooh!

00:02:30.297 --> 00:02:31.193
- Eat.

00:02:31.193 --> 00:02:33.873
(perky music)

00:02:33.873 --> 00:02:35.704
- Something sweet is in here.

00:02:35.704 --> 00:02:37.094
I'm not mad at it.

00:02:37.094 --> 00:02:37.945
- No.

00:02:37.945 --> 00:02:39.847
- It's like dessert Chipotle.

00:02:39.847 --> 00:02:40.792
- Yeah, I don't like it.

00:02:40.792 --> 00:02:42.397
(laughing)

00:02:42.397 --> 00:02:43.666
- Yeah, that's really good!

00:02:43.666 --> 00:02:44.499
- I'm a fan.

00:02:44.499 --> 00:02:46.106
- This is banging!

00:02:46.106 --> 00:02:48.675
Especially when you get like

00:02:48.675 --> 00:02:50.840
the zest from the lemon

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:51.673
like

00:02:51.673 --> 00:02:53.714
(perky music)

00:02:53.714 --> 00:02:54.791
this (beeping) is popping.

00:02:54.791 --> 00:02:55.838
- I just wish it wasn't so slimy.

00:02:55.838 --> 00:02:57.647
It's just slipping all
over my hands right now.

00:02:57.647 --> 00:02:59.211
- Like I said, something that you do

00:02:59.211 --> 00:03:00.389
with your close friends.

00:03:00.389 --> 00:03:01.344
- Exactly.

00:03:01.344 --> 00:03:03.242
- Ooh, now it's kinda like sweet and spicy

00:03:03.242 --> 00:03:04.581
when it like sits on your tongue.

00:03:04.581 --> 00:03:05.489
- It was definitely--

00:03:05.489 --> 00:03:07.031
- Ooh, I like that!

00:03:07.031 --> 00:03:07.864
- Yeah.

00:03:07.864 --> 00:03:08.697
- The sauce is really good.

00:03:08.697 --> 00:03:09.657
- I can feel it in the back of my throat.

00:03:09.657 --> 00:03:10.828
(perky music)

00:03:10.828 --> 00:03:11.875
- It's a little spicy but--

00:03:11.875 --> 00:03:12.708
- A tiny bit.

00:03:12.708 --> 00:03:15.736
- I'm Nigerian so it's
really not that spicy.

00:03:15.736 --> 00:03:17.585
- A good mix of like sweet,

00:03:17.585 --> 00:03:19.556
like a tangy zest situation happening

00:03:19.556 --> 00:03:20.755
because of the lemon,

00:03:20.755 --> 00:03:21.871
savory.

00:03:21.871 --> 00:03:23.628
It's a spicy something happening

00:03:23.628 --> 00:03:24.482
but it's not too much.

00:03:24.482 --> 00:03:26.491
It's like the right amount of each.

00:03:26.491 --> 00:03:28.028
It not flavor overkill.

00:03:28.028 --> 00:03:31.462
(lively, bass-thumping music)

00:03:31.462 --> 00:03:33.665
- This is outside-of-the-box
Chipotle work here.

00:03:33.665 --> 00:03:35.819
- I think you're on to something.

00:03:35.819 --> 00:03:36.684
- The sweet is perfect.

00:03:36.684 --> 00:03:38.661
It just needs to like jack up on the spicy

00:03:38.661 --> 00:03:39.650
just a little bit.

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:41.628
- Now I'm going to go to Chipotle

00:03:41.628 --> 00:03:44.124
instead of Dos Toros.

00:03:44.124 --> 00:03:44.957
Good job, Jade.

00:03:44.957 --> 00:03:46.348
- Oh, yeah.

00:03:46.348 --> 00:03:47.181
(laughing)

00:03:47.181 --> 00:03:48.061
- In order for me to eat this,

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:50.600
I would remove the agave.

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:54.249
That's the thing that
like really threw me off.

00:03:54.249 --> 00:03:56.301
I still love Chipotle though.

00:03:56.301 --> 00:03:58.515
I'm never gonna give that up probably.

00:03:58.515 --> 00:04:03.075
- I am now forever indebted
to my awesome co-worker, Jade.

00:04:03.075 --> 00:04:05.452
- I just want to thank you for
introducing this to my life.

00:04:05.452 --> 00:04:07.577
It's definitely changed it for the better.

00:04:07.577 --> 00:04:08.410
- Yeah.

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:10.857
- Even Chipotle salads are
better than eating salad.

00:04:10.857 --> 00:04:12.921
- Um, that's a quote.

00:04:12.921 --> 00:04:14.026
(laughing)

00:04:14.026 --> 00:04:16.526
(perky music)

